// ─── LEAGUE BASELINES (engine v3) ────────────────────────────────────────────
// Everything the engine needs to know about a sport lives in this one table. Provenance of each number:
//   [S] looked up in a published source while building this version
//   [A] approximate long-run value from standard references, not re-verified here (refresh when you can)
//   [J] a judgement about how far to trust a stat (shrinkage, weights); not a measured quantity
// L      league average scored per team per game (team ratings are measured against it). A route-supplied
//        league average for the current season replaces it when one is found (see leagueL).
// hfa    home edge in the final margin (pts/goals/runs). Zero at a neutral venue.
// fam    scoring distribution: nb = negative binomial (MLB), pois = Poisson (NHL, soccer), norm = correlated normal.
// sdM/sdT  SD of the final margin / total (norm family). r = NB size. otF = share of a game played in overtime.
// k, rho   shrinkage: a team's rate is worth k games of league-average evidence; rho = year-to-year persistence.
// gpDef    games played assumed when neither the routes nor the record say. season = games in a full season.
// omega    share of the opposing defence that is the starter on the day (pitcher, goalie, keeper).
// lgGK/lgSv  league baseline for the starter stat. kGK = starter shrinkage (IP or starts). qbK = rating-point value of a QB.
// wEff     weight of opponent-adjusted efficiency ratings next to raw scoring (higher where schedules differ most).
